/* The eight handlers are NOT eight copies of one wrapper, which is what the M5
   spec's outline suggested.  Read from the image, they come in four shapes:

     type 0 $AF31   CALL $B028 unconditionally, then set the sprite
     types 1, 5     BIT 1,(IY+7) / CALL z,$B028 -- the walk is GATED
     types 2,3,6,7  rescale the step or patch the walker first: type 3 halves
                    ($B610 SRL), type 7 DOUBLES it (SLA on both bytes -- which
                    is the measured "fast walker"), type 6 patches $B20D/$B25D
                    to $C9 so the ledge test returns instead of hopping
     type 4 $AF77   CALL $B3C5, a different routine entirely

   Only the first two shapes are transliterated here; 'gate' says how the walker
   is reached and null means NOT YET DONE.  A scene containing one of those five
   is held out of the walker gate and counted, not quietly passed. */
/* WHAT EACH HANDLER DOES, read off $AF31-$B027 and measured by calling all
   eight directly (build/walker_fixture.json, the 'handlers' block).
     walk            $AF31          CALL $B028, UNCONDITIONAL
     walk + gate     $AF47 / $AF5F  BIT 1,(IY+7) / CALL z,$B028
     fly             $AF95 / $AFAF  ($B611) from ($B610) -- HALVED by type 3's
                                    lone SRL -- then CALL $B26F, a 2-D flyer
                                    that is not the walker at all
     null                           not transliterated; DECLINED OUTRIGHT, and
                                    test/bb.test.js asserts it writes nothing
   'always' vs 'bit1' is invisible in any capture of a running round, because
   the spawner clears bit 1 ($7455 RES 1) and nothing that runs sets it -- it
   took a direct call with the bit SET to tell them apart.  And for types 2 and
   3 that same bit is not a gate at all: $B2B0 reads it as the Y DIRECTION. */
const BB_ENEMY_MOVE = [
  { move: 'walk' },                                // 0 $AF31
  { move: 'walk', gate: 'bit1' },                  // 1 $AF47
  { move: 'fly',  vstep: 'copy' },                 // 2 $AF95
  { move: 'fly',  vstep: 'half' },                 // 3 $AFAF -- SRL, so 1 px down
  { move: 'hop4', tail: 'clampY' },                // 4 $AF77 -> $B3C5
  { move: 'walk', gate: 'bit1' },                  // 5 $AF5F
  { move: 'walk', patch: 'ledge', flip: 0xB008 },  // 6 $AFF6
  { move: 'walk', patch: 'all',   scale: 'double' },  // 7 $AFC4
];

